# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Seán R. Kavanagh et al. (2026). Fast and Accurate Equivariant Foundation Models for Atomistic Simulation.
#   arXiv (Cornell University). doi:10.48550/arxiv.2607.28461  arXiv:2607.28461v2
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2607.28461v2 (sha256 06c42ef66879ac1c...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 690 (Method/model). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/kavanagh2026.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the NequIP and Allegro foundation models trained in the
# paper on MPtrj (MP) and on OAM (OMat24 pre-training followed by MPA
# fine-tuning), with hyperparameters from Table 1 and the Matbench
# Discovery energy-above-hull MAEs on the WBM test set (Table 2).
# Geometry RMSDs, thermal conductivity, heat capacity, force-softening
# ratios, phonon and MatCalc benchmarks are property results. DIRECT and
# MPA-only models appear only in figures.

